Package: qxBuilder
Type: Package
Title: Build and Populate Qualtrics Surveys from R and JSON Templates
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Robin", "Shanholtz", email = "robinshanholtz95@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A thin wrapper around the Qualtrics Survey Definitions API for
    programmatically creating survey blocks and questions, and for driving
    that creation from a JSON template file. Grew out of a series of
    hand-written scripts for adding blank Text Entry and interactive
    "Highlight" questions to a Qualtrics survey; generalizes that work into
    reusable, testable building blocks. Question-type support is split into
    two confidence tiers, documented per-function: types verified against a
    live Qualtrics account (Text Entry, Highlight), and best-effort types
    built from Qualtrics's documented schema but not yet exercised against a
    live API call (Multiple Choice, Matrix) -- see the "Confidence" section
    of each question builder's documentation.
